{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"f78807782e3aa414f6a3ca384fc2fe19100a982e79350719316e64b6fd7a5bc4","digest":{"component_or_area":"sync reconciliation and detached-HEAD handling","key_entities":["src/rebar/_store/sync.py:95","sync.reconverge()","_do_reconverge","reset --hard","refs/heads/tickets","tests/unit/test_sync_union_recovery.py","git checkout --detach"],"problem_keywords":["detached HEAD","local-ahead","sync","data loss","regression test","reconvergence","union merge"],"propositions":["A tracker worktree can enter a detached-HEAD-local-ahead state where HEAD advances past a local commit but refs/heads/tickets remains at the base, creating a diverged merge scenario.","The sync reconvergence must measure local-ahead by HEAD (not the branch ref) to preserve local commits in detached-HEAD state; measuring by the lagging branch ref would incorrectly trigger reset --hard and orphan the local commit.","After sync.reconverge() completes on a detached-HEAD-local-ahead repo, both the local event commit and the remote event commit must remain reachable from HEAD and both event directories must exist in the working tree.","A regression test must reproduce the detached-HEAD-local-ahead state (tracker cloned from origin at base, origin advanced, tracker detached and locally committed, both sides ahead) and assert local commit survival through reconvergence."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785823638427101432,"uuid":"7dc9bd60-64d8-4ae2-9e2f-065aa016b677"}